#5810
A Black Sand Beach~
   Black volcanic sand crunches underfoot along this narrow beach, and
the surf of the Sea of Tears rolls in white over a reef offshore.
Behind the beach the jungle of the Isle of Karras rises like a wall: a
dense, steaming tangle of palms, ferns and creeper-hung trees, loud with
the shrieks of birds.  A few minotaur-sized dugout canoes have been
dragged up above the tide line.  The sea lies to the west, and a path
enters the jungle to the east.
~
