#5814
A Steaming Stream~
   A stream runs across the trail here, so warm that steam curls from
its surface, and the stones in its bed are slick with bright green weed.
The water smells faintly of sulfur.  Tiny brilliantly colored frogs
cling to the stones, and you would be wise not to touch them.  The trail
continues east and west, and a ruin is visible through the trees to the
north.
