#5821
Before the Gates of Karras~
   The paved road ends before the gates of Karras, two massive doors of
iron-bound timber set into walls of gray stone so finely fitted that no
mortar was needed to build them.  Above the gate a great double axe has
been carved into the stone, one blade chiseled smooth and the other left
rough.  The gates lead east into the fortress, and the road leads back
down the hill to the west.
